{# The backup codes of a second factor, shown this once (architecture §5.2): the codes, the way to take
   them in one click, and what each one is worth.

   One file for the two pages that show them, the enrolment and the renewal, because what a person has to
   do with them is the same thing both times: put them somewhere safe before they leave the page. They are
   stored hashed, so nothing shows them again.

   The button that copies them is hidden until the script of the provider finds a browser that can write a
   clipboard (copy.js); the codes are on the page either way, as text somebody selects. #}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}
<ol id="backup-codes" data-two-factor="backup-codes" data-codes="{{ backup_codes|length }}">
    {% for code in backup_codes %}
        <li><code>{{ code }}</code></li>
    {% endfor %}
</ol>
<p data-copy-refused hidden>{{ 'two_factor.backup_codes.not_copied'|trans }}</p>
